findings.body:
**A partial review now hides a failing check behind `pr/ci-pending`.**

The new partial-review branch comes before the failing-check scan, so it returns before that scan runs:

```js
// A quick or area-restricted pass is no merge signal.
if (review?.state === "success" && review.description?.startsWith("partial review")) {
  return "pr/ci-pending";
}
```

https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/4992366cf65b25c8a918fddfec55d271a87a2a37/.github/workflows/pr-status.yml#L155-L158

When a partial round has no importants, the poster sets `success` / `partial review: no blocking issues` (`tools/review/src/post-review.script.ts:232-237`). Nothing in `claude-code-review.yml` waits for CI before it runs, so the owner can request a quick or area-restricted review on a head whose tests already failed. That PR then gets `pr/ci-pending` ("Checks are still running") instead of `pr/ci-failing`, because the scan at lines 165-172 never runs:

https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/4992366cf65b25c8a918fddfec55d271a87a2a37/.github/workflows/pr-status.yml#L165-L172

This breaks the file header's own order (`pr/review-open > pr/ci-failing > pr/ci-pending > pr/ready`, lines 2-4), and it tells the author to wait when something needs fixing.

The goal, "a partial review is no merge signal", only requires that a partial review never reaches `pr/ready`. Delete lines 155-158 and move the condition into the pending check:

```js
const running = combined.statuses.some(
  (s) => s.state === "pending" && !s.description?.startsWith("Not reviewed"),
);
// A quick or area-restricted pass is no merge signal.
const partial = review?.state === "success" && review.description?.startsWith("partial review");
if (runs.some((c) => c.status !== "completed") || running || partial) {
  return "pr/ci-pending";
}
```
